# TEST_MODE : MULTI_MODULE_OK

# Tuple types across SEPARATELY COMPILED modules.
#
# A tuple is interned per module -- nothing is written down and nothing is
# shared. Both modules independently re-derive the type from its element types,
# and the mangled name has to come out identical or the link fails:
#
#     undefined reference to `TakePair(FBTUPLE2<int, int>)'
#
# The two modules deliberately spell the SAME tuple with DIFFERENT element
# names, because element names must not reach the type. Nothing in the
# single-module suite can catch either failure, which is why this is a .bmk.

MAIN := tuple-mm-main.bas
SRCS := tuple-mm-a.bas
